A||||17||loafer87gt||Bloody Car Thieves!!!! Argghhh!||||1||
Z||000000||loafer87gt||05-06-2000||03:45 PM||||I woke out of bed this morning to find my Gt had been broken into AGAIN!! The bastards took all of my stereo equipment including my new Clarion CD player, my new custom sub box,trashed my center console again, and bled all over seats. Jeez, I've had it, I'm not going to bother trying to put another stereo in my car. What a downer, i bet my equipment has already depreciated to 50% of its original value in the past 5 months that I got the new equipment. This is the second time in the past year that I have had my car stolen and had all of my equipment ripped off. I wish I could catch the bastard in the act and bust his damn kneecaps. So my question is, what is the best place to get a good condition center console? Later guys||||reg||1
Z||000001||FieroGTGirl||05-06-2000||03:52 PM||||I am sorry to hear that.  <P>Do you have an alarm?  What color is the console?  I may have a spare!<P>Hope the day goes better.||||reg||9
Z||000002||GT Bastard||05-06-2000||04:08 PM||||Damn Loafer.... Don't lose hope.  The karma police will catch the filthy bastards eventually.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||8
Z||000003||Carolina 88GT||05-06-2000||04:51 PM||||Catch the bas**** on a time lapse video or something....||||reg||1
Z||000004||fierosound||05-06-2000||04:56 PM||||I hear ya!!!!   I was living in a townhouse  with your usual open parking.  One morning, I go out on my way to work and the car is GONE!  It was found a couple days later, all the stereo equipment ripped out of it and damaged dash, console etc.  I had everything replaced (covered by insurance) and got an even better system!<P>Thirteen months later, SAME THING!!  Go out in the morning GONE!!  My townhouse was up for sale two weeks later.  I bought a house with a double-attached front garage before I installed the system I have in the car now. It's never on the street overnight, and I have secure underground parking at work. I also installed a honkin' LOUD alarm system!!<P>I hope things work out for ya - I made sure they did for me.  PS - high end stuff only depreciates 20% a year.  If it's less than a year, full replacement with is covered - at least it was with my policy.  Yours may vary.  <BR> <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fierosound" TARGET=_blank>www.geocities.com/fierosound</A> <BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierosound (edited 05-06-2000).]||||reg||8
Z||000005||phillip||05-06-2000||05:24 PM||||how many times has this happened? do you think it could be some one you know? maybe you could start again and be as stealthy as possible. like a small sub and some bass shakers under the seat. or if you could get the radio far enough into the dash putting a false face over it.<P>go slow enough to work out how to protect each piece as best you can. but, if it is people you know (hate to seem paranoid but if it keeps happening you have to wonder if some one knows something) this may not help. permanence of mounting will slow them down though.||||reg||1
Z||000006||loafer87gt||05-06-2000||05:59 PM||||Hye guys, the police just came over and I filed my report. I guess five other vehicles were broken into last night. My buddy down the street had his Iroc broken into as well, they smashed his hatch and grabbed his headunit. This is the second time my car has been stolen. The first time someone stole it and took it for a joyride and smashed up the frontend, and did a lot of damage to the back lid when they used a crowbar to pry it open. This time the guys who broken in were "nice enough" to use the electric hatch release and didn't trash my decklid. Guys, I am so worn out. This car just seems to be an ongoing saga of problems. I think the quote "They were the best of times, and the worst fo times" sums up my time with my Fiero. I can't seem to part with it though as, for as weird as this sounds, I am in love with it. It was my first car I ever bought and absolutely baby it. It just really hurts when I see someone voilate my car like this. The only thing that makes me feel better is knowing that in the end these assclowns will have to explain their actions to the man upstairs come judgement day! I'll keep you guys posted on what happens. In the meantime, I am going to look at getting a used subwoofer assembly from a Fiero and work on putting my own soundstream sub in it. Later guys||||reg||1
Z||000007||Oreif||05-06-2000||09:32 PM||||Time to get an alarm system! It's usually a good deterent for stereo thieves! ||||reg||1
Z||000008||Racer 1||05-06-2000||11:38 PM||||Get a VIPER alarm. My viper alarm has soft touch plus I have a motion sensor under the middle console so if anybody sticks there hands in my car while the windows are down the alarm will go off. I also have the viper voice "proteced by security system stand back" "system armed and disarmed". It also helps to have NRA stickers front and back although my cars stays in the garage if its out front and some punks needs to learn the hard way not to theive stuff. I have a remington 7mm rem mag I can sniper him off at 500-1000 yards clean. <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by Racer 1 (edited 05-06-2000).]||||reg||10
Z||000009||stimpy||05-07-2000||10:57 AM||||An alarm will be my next major purchase. Unfortunately,many people ignore alarms these days. That is why I plan on installing at least two pain-generating sirens inside the car.  If they want my deck badly enough to actually get it out, their ears are gonna be bleeding!<P>Loafer sorry for your loss.  I know what it is like to be violated like that. Can make ya really want to hurt someone.||||reg||1
Z||000010||deceler8||05-07-2000||11:13 AM||||You could get a 2m4 with stock steel wheels and Delco Radio...<P>I would never put big bucks into a '80's GM car with frameless doors...learned my lesson with my Olds Cutlass...<P>These are the easiest cars to break into...almost takes longer to use the key than a coat hanger or slim jim.||||reg||1
Z||000011||Sillhouette.com||05-07-2000||07:27 PM||||Your best bet is a good alarm.  Mine is one built by Clifford for South African market.  It has a pager that works in the Ontario region.  The way it works is if there is a carjack in progress just get out of the car call up this number and spell kill into the beep and the fuel will be shut off anytime the car is below 20 KPH.  Another function is the under door flame thrower.  Too bad that is illegal here in Canada.  It works by pressing a button and two 12' flames will shoot out at a 45 degree angle underneath the doors (both sides) another carjacking invention that is also usable if anyone forces the door open.  I think there is only two of these alarms here on this side of the pond<P>Later...<P>||||reg||3
Z||000012||Dan86gt3.8||05-08-2000||12:41 AM||||you said assclowns?  as in no talent assclowns?  you know like Micheal Bolton.  Ohhh by the way do you work at initech?||||reg||7
Z||000013||Standard||05-08-2000||01:21 AM||||speaking of alarms.. I set off another one with the exhaust note on my GT today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">... that makes 3 so far..||||reg||1
Z||000014||LarryB||05-08-2000||01:33 AM||||There are a number of good alarms, if you're going to go that route at the very least get one with motion sensors and ignition kill.  If you're willing to lay out $500-600 look into something like a LOJACK, <A HREF="http://www.lojack.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.lojack.com</A>  <P>I'd say a 160 gr. bullet from a 7MM Remington Magnum to the lower groin area would about even the score with a thieving little puke but the cops would probably have a small problem with it.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000015||fierospeeder||05-08-2000||02:39 AM||||i seen in jc whitney along time ago, kill switches for your battery, hide the switch someplace that cant be found, like underneath the seat, or be creative enough and rig up your dome light button.  Something i guess that bypasses the ignition wire going to the starter.  <P>I seen these new Clubs for the wheels that are electric, you get a shock.  Im not sure if it has actually been marketed. <BR>||||reg||1
Z||000016||stsmithgt||05-08-2000||01:22 PM|||| <A HREF="http://securityplanet.com/54000.htm" TARGET=_blank>http://securityplanet.com/54000.htm</A>      Try typing in this address to see a auto tasor club that I think costs about 200.00.  It also has an ear piercing noise too.  I'm very tempted to get one, but my car has been such a money pit lately, I don't have the extra cash laying around.  I think I've sunk about 1000.00 dollars in this last month and now I lost a motor to a headlight and a clutch slave cylinder seems to be acting up.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/mad.gif"> It still didn't ruin my weekend of boating at Lake Nacimiento. <BR>t||||reg||14
Z||000017||fiero56||05-08-2000||02:00 PM||||I've had my Viper alarm system in my Fiero for about a year now. It works great, no false alarms yet, and it came with a pager. I don't use the pager much, just leave it on the sun visor, but the alarm has been nice to have. It gives me a little more peace of mind having starter kill, etc. I plan to have two very loud sirens installed under the dash sometime this summer(same time I upgrade from stock stereo).<P>My only suggestion is have a COMPETANT shop do the installation. The morons that installed mine, probably still remember my bitching. I made them fix their installation 4 times before I was satisfied. Now I know of a very good shop that does my alarm work. <P><BR>Dan, thats a great movie!!! OFFICE SPACE!!! <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 05-08-2000).]||||reg||1
